        "naphtha",
        "wti"
      ],
      "intensity": "Raw materials ~45% of tire cost of goods; natural rubber 22% of raw-material spend, synthetic rubber 22%, carbon black 16%, pigments/oils/chemicals 21%, wire/other 11%, fabric 8%; about two-thirds of raw materials are petroleum based. The company's own sensitivity: a 1% move in natural rubber is ~$8M a year, with a 4 to 6 month lag",
